# DATABASE_URL: PostgreSQL connection string.
# Backs leads, first-party analytics (Visitor/Session/PageView/Event) and the
# instant site audit (SiteAudit). Required — the app runs without it, but every
# write falls back to leads.json and nothing is queryable.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/optimizeindex"

# PORT: HTTP port for the Express server. Defaults to 3000.
# Production runs on 3002 behind nginx (see ecosystem.config.cjs).
PORT="3000"

# PAGESPEED_API_KEY: Google PageSpeed Insights API key.
# Powers the Core Web Vitals half of the homepage instant audit.
# Strongly recommended: without a key Google rate-limits the endpoint so
# aggressively that most visitors get no speed data at all. Free to create at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (enable the "PageSpeed
# Insights API"), and free for 25,000 requests/day.
# The audit degrades gracefully when this is absent — the other three
# categories still score, and the speed card says it wasn't measured.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=""

# SESSION_SECRET: signing key for admin session cookies. REQUIRED in production
# — the server refuses to start without it rather than issue sessions it cannot
# verify. Must be at least 32 characters. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
# Rotating this value invalidates every signed-in admin session, which is how
# you force a logout everywhere.
# In development a random per-process value is used if this is unset, so `npm
# run dev` works out of the box; restarting just signs you out.
SESSION_SECRET=""
